  "notes": "The distinctive here is a melody that is dense and narrow at the same time: the research says the vocal is speech-dense with short sung tags rather than full sung hooks — high syllable density, low melodic range — so this file carries a high `densityPerBar` over the narrowest melodic register in the batch (63–84, 21 semitones) with the highest step share here at 0.78 and `octaveJumpProb` down at 0.05. Nothing else on this axis pairs those two. The harmony is the mournful pair the research names, i–VI–III–VII and i–VII–VI–V, the second of which no other entry here uses. `pitched_vocal_chop` is the palette's third element beside piano and nylon guitar. ⚠ `arrangement.transitions.dropOutBeats` is raised to 4 beats at 0.85 because the research names drum drop-outs as the main dynamic device and says the drums are often muted for whole verse bars — a full-bar mute is out of the vocabulary's reach, so a 4-beat drop at high probability is the nearest honest thing, and the number is INFERRED. ⚠ `medium` per the research's own rating. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
